#: includes/admin-page.php:1451
msgid "About Accessibility"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1453
msgid "The Typography Stylist block is built for accessibility. It makes two versions of each heading: a plain text version for screen readers and a styled version for sighted readers."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1454
msgid "The settings below control how screen readers and other assistive technologies handle styled text. The defaults suit most sites. Change them only if your site has specific accessibility requirements."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1459
msgid "Built-in Accessibility Features"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1460
msgid "These features work with no setup:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1462
msgid "Typography Stylist Block:"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the attribute aria-hidden="true", shown as code.
#: includes/admin-page.php:1465
#, php-format
msgid "Makes two headings. Screen readers get a plain text version that is visually hidden. Sighted readers get the styled version, which %s hides from screen readers."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1469
msgid "Inline Format (Rich Text Blocks):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1469
msgid "Applies the styling directly to the text. Screen readers read the text as it is."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1476
msgid "Inline Format Settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1477
msgid "This setting applies to text styled with the inline format in standard blocks, such as headings and paragraphs."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1483
msgid "Disable Word Boundary Warning"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1494
#: includes/class-typost-admin-options.php:70
msgid "Skip the warning when applying features to partial words"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1497
msgid "When you style part of a word (for example, one letter) with the inline format, the editor shows a warning and offers to convert the text to a Typography Stylist block. Turn this on to skip the warning and apply the styling directly."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1506
msgid "Save Accessibility Settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1513
msgid "Accessibility Best Practices"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1515
msgid "To style part of a word, use the Typography Stylist block, not the inline format."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1516
msgid "With the inline format, select complete words or phrases. A styled part of a word can make a screen reader read the word in pieces."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1517
msgid "Test styled headings with a screen reader, such as NVDA on Windows or VoiceOver on macOS."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1518
msgid "If you style part of a word with the inline format, the editor warns you and offers to convert the text to a Typography Stylist block. You can turn off this warning above."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1535
msgid "About Replacement Fonts"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1537
msgid "Font replacements ensure your content looks correct even after deleting a font. When a font is removed, any content that used it would normally lose its styling. Replacement mappings redirect that content to display with a different font instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1538
msgid "Replacements are created automatically when you delete a font and choose a replacement. You can also create them manually for fonts that were deleted before this feature was available."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1542
msgid "When a font is deleted, you can map it to a replacement font. Content using the deleted font will automatically display with the replacement."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1546
#: typography-stylist.php:1541
msgid "No font replacements configured."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1550
msgid "Add New Replacement Mapping"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1551
msgid "Manually create a replacement mapping for a font ID that was previously deleted."
msgstr ""

